---
const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'Do I need an account?',
    answer: 'No. FridgeShare does not use hosted accounts. Editing is granted by the full board URL with its token fragment.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can I share a read-only link?',
    answer: 'Yes. Share the board URL without the #token fragment and people can view without editing.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can I run it on my own server or NAS?',
    answer: 'That is the intended path. Docker Compose is the recommended setup, and the default data volume keeps board files and uploads on your hardware.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What should I do before exposing it publicly?',
    answer: 'Set SELFHOST_ADMIN_TOKEN first so board creation and deletion are not left open, then make sure the mounted data directory is being backed up.',
  },
];
---
<section id="faq" class="bg-white px-6 py-20 sm:py-28">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
    <div class="text-center">
      <span class="inline-flex rounded-full border border-honey-200 bg-honey-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-honey-600">
        FAQ
      </span>
      <h2 class="mt-5 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-warm-900 sm:text-4xl">Short answers before you click away</h2>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-warm-700">
        Enough detail to remove the obvious uncertainty. The rest lives in the docs.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 space-y-4">
      {faqs.map((faq) => (
        <div class="rounded-3xl border border-warm-200 bg-warm-50 p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-warm-900">{faq.question}</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-warm-700 sm:text-base">{faq.answer}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
